  "lesson": "## Tiny, fast, tense\n\nFader open. For the first two beats of each bar, shake the jog forward and back as fast as it will go: sixteen tiny strokes in two beats, sixteenth-note triplet speed, then rest for two beats. The strokes are millimetres long and come from the fingers, not the wrist.\n\nThe scribble is a tension sound: it sits on a snare or a vocal and buzzes. The scorer wants sixteen direction changes in the window and does not care how far the platter moves, so keep the movement small; big movements slow you down and lose the grid. Two beats on, two beats off, for the whole drill.\n",
